    {
      "title": "Repeat offenders, and which specific resource is being fought over",
      "type": "text",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 7,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 39
      },
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "**Not evidenced**, and the largest real gap on this board. The charter's definitive fight signal is a *specific resource instance* corrected on 90%+ of runs, or corrected 5 or more times in a week: an agent, a package post-install, or a human with sudo and a habit, rewriting the same `Package[nginx]` on the same three nodes between every Puppet run. `puppet_change_events` cannot answer that: it is fleet-wide by resource *type*, not by resource *title* or by node, and it is read from each node's latest report rather than tracked across runs. Closing this needs a new per-resource, per-node correction counter, which is a collector change, not a dashboard one."
      },
      "id": 1847549499
    },
